---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-05-25';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Now"
  description="What I'm focused on right now."
>
  <article class="prose-essay">
    <header class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <h1 class="text-[40px] font-semibold tracking-tight">Now</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-faint)] font-mono">
        Updated {updated} · what I&rsquo;m focused on this month
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15.5px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        Inspired by Derek Sivers&rsquo;
        <a href="https://nownownow.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">/now</a> convention.
        Not a status feed. More like &mdash; if we caught up over coffee, this is what I&rsquo;d say
        I&rsquo;m working on.
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>Building</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Zyberpol agent eval framework.</strong> Designing how we measure correctness
        for the Correlation and Investigation agents when there&rsquo;s no single right
        trajectory. See <a href="/writing/evaluating-multi-agent-systems/">the essay</a> for
        the broad shape.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>RAG infrastructure for security context.</strong> Alert history, runbooks,
        threat intel, environment graph. The retrieval quality is what makes the agents
        useful or useless.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Drafting a follow-up to the multi-agent eval essay on golden trajectories.</li>
      <li>Working on a short piece on RAG eval limits &mdash; what Ragas and Phoenix don&rsquo;t cover.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reading</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Whatever new agent/eval paper got dropped this week.</li>
      <li>Going slowly through Lilian Weng&rsquo;s LLM-agent writeups again with current production eyes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Not doing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Twitter/X. Job interviews. Side projects unrelated to VEZRAN.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
